   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Computer hardware is grouped by information processing: input devices enter data, the CPU processes it, storage devices keep it, and output devices show it. The CPU has a control unit, an ALU and registers. Storage is primary (RAM, ROM, CMOS) or secondary (tape, disk, CD, DVD)."
    }
